{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg9xY9oicimf6qHBBdpDG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I changed `Hijack` in `response_writer.go` so it only refuses when body bytes have already been written (`size > 0`). Before, it refused as soon as anything was written (`w.Written()`), which included sending just the headers. That blocked websocket libraries (e.g. coder/websocket) that write the response header and then hijack the connection.\n\nThe error message is now \"gin: response body already written\". I also added a test case, \"hijack after header write should succeed\", to `TestResponseWriterHijackAfterWrite`.\n\nThe gate check passed: the new test fails without the fix and passes with it, and format and whitespace checks are clean. I only ran the `TestResponseWriterHijack*` tests, not the full suite, and I didn't try it against a real websocket library."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1222,"cache_read_input_tokens":33141,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1222,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"15f97229-dd9a-4ede-b367-f6516be4fad4","uuid":"56ac8664-1c01-4b3d-aaf3-59b13e8e7140","timestamp":"2026-10-18T15:42:59.356Z","request_id":"req_011Cg9xY9aq2fxBTHQgXtpcS"}
